{
  "$comment": "Every API-key operation both SDKs wrap, and its route class (contract 02 §4). The class decides what may be retried: `safe` — no charge, and a repeat changes nothing the first call did not (every GET, run cancel, member resolve, and the free idempotent writes: list rename, list item add and remove, feedback vote), retried whenever the outcome allows; `billed` — charged once the work is done (the CSV exports too: free today, but the server prices them through the same meter once export pricing ships); the server recognises a same-day repeat with the same Idempotency-Key that returns the same rows, but one that returns different rows is charged for them, so a request that may have been sent is never repeated; `keyed` — the server requires Idempotency-Key, so a repeat with the same key is recognised and safe; `once` — free, but a repeat is not the same as one call: it files a duplicate (feedback, a new list) or answers differently (deleting a list twice says 404 the second time). The retry decisions per class are in retry-policy.json. The operation list is openapi.json's: every operation whose security includes APIKeyHeader, plus the public GET /v1/feedback/tags the SDKs also wrap. A test fails if an API-key operation in openapi.json is neither classified here nor listed under not_wrapped.",
  "version": 1,
